std::abs is not a function template for floating-point types. libc++ 21
only provides integer overloads as templates, so std::abs<Real>(x) fails
to compile. Introduced in 68d3844a / 5ab87cdc (2012) while silencing
conversion warnings. Call std::abs without an explicit template argument.

--- a/modules/geom/src/quat.cc	2026-08-15 16:53:31
+++ b/modules/geom/src/quat.cc	2026-08-15 16:53:31
@@ -133,9 +133,9 @@
